---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';

// /metadax/guide/next-session/ -- session two from the next-time note, the
// learning record, and several children at once. Tracks SKILL.md steps 5 and 6,
// the player's "save to a learning record (download only)", the learner-record
// template repo, and the learners[] multi-learner shape.
---
<Base title="Session two, the learning record, and several kids — Meta DAX" description="Build the next session straight from the note the page leaves, keep a dated learning record on your own machine, and teach more than one child from one package." wide>
  <section class="lede">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/metadax/">Meta DAX</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/metadax/guide/">Help</a> &rsaquo; Next session</p>
    <h1>Session two, and several kids</h1>
    <p class="lede-text">
      One lesson is a start. The point is the next one, and the one after. Here is
      how to keep going &mdash; from the note the page leaves, the record you keep,
      and teaching more than one child at once.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-next">
    <h2 id="h-next">Session two, from the next-time note</h2>
    <p class="body">
      The learner page leaves a short <strong>next-time note</strong> &mdash; a few
      lines about how the session went. When you come back, give that note to the
      skill or the AI chat (paste it in, or point it at the file you saved) and ask
      for the next session. It builds session two straight from it:
    </p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>it keeps what worked, and opens with a callback to it rather than starting over;</li>
      <li>it moves one step on from the stuck spot &mdash; one step, never a leap &mdash; and never repeats a thing the note says already failed;</li>
      <li>it changes the game&rsquo;s theme only if the note says your child tired of it;</li>
      <li>it paces the length and tone to how the last one ended.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body">
      It keeps a small <code>family-progress.json</code> on your own machine so it
      remembers where you are next time. That file is private and is never
      uploaded.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-record">
    <h2 id="h-record">The learning record</h2>
    <p class="body">
      A learning record is one short, dated entry per session that you add to over
      time &mdash; readable by you and by a program. There are two easy ways to keep
      one:
    </p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>In the player, at the end of a session, you are offered the chance to <strong>save that session to a learning record</strong>. It downloads a file to your device; nothing is uploaded.</li>
      <li>Or, after you have actually run the session, the skill (or AI chat) can write a record entry for you: which games you played, the slips that kept coming up &mdash; described as behaviour, never as a label &mdash; something your child said, and your own note on the hardest moment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="body">
      The record stays on your machine. If you ever want to keep it in its own
      place, there is a template repository you can copy; it stays private until
      you choose, in one step, to publish it.
    </p>
    <p class="out"><a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/metadax-learner-record">The learning-record template &rarr;</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="h-many">
    <h2 id="h-many">Several children at once</h2>
    <p class="body">
      If more than one child does the same lesson together, you answer the
      questions <strong>once for the group</strong> &mdash; a nickname and a rough
      age for each child &mdash; not once per child. The package then carries each
      child, and every part shows who does it: one child reads a part, the little
      ones do the hands-on part, the oldest gets the explaining part. In the player
      and in print, a small label on each part says whose it is.
    </p>
    <p class="body">
      Adding another child to the family later, or the same child on a new subject,
      reuses what you already answered &mdash; you are not interviewed from scratch.
    </p>
    <p class="out">
      <a href="/metadax/guide/share/">Next: share a sample &rarr;</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
      <a href="/metadax/guide/">Back to the guide</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { padding-block: 3rem 2rem; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .eyebrow a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .eyebrow a:hover, .eyebrow a:focus-visible { color: var(--fg); }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.2rem + 2.6vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.22; letter-spacing: -0.012em; max-width: 20em; text-wrap: balance; }
  .lede-text { margin: 0; max-width: 40em; color: #cfcfcf; }

  .block { padding-block: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); }
  .body { margin: 0; max-width: 40em; color: #cfcfcf; }
  .body + .body, .body + .out, .out + .body, .body + .plain, .plain + .body { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .body a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .body a:hover, .body a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
  .plain { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; max-width: 42em; color: #cfcfcf; }
  .plain li + li { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 8%, transparent); padding: 0.1em 0.35em; border-radius: 4px; }

  .out { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .out span { color: var(--faint); margin-inline: 0.5rem; }
  .out a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .out a:hover, .out a:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
</style>
